s diff is recorded for A4-2.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4475,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A3 is reversible because the read path canonicalizes both shapes idempotently' — the read path referenced is the new/normalizing one","POST-ROLLBACK overlay applies: A3 is an in-place reinterpretation of existing persisted records (baseline value shape), not a purely-additive optional field","The plan's reverse-direction rollback artifact is scoped to A4-2 only ('reverting A4-2 requires the reverse-direction corpus diff'); no equivalent post-rollback interpretation assertion is recorded for A3's already-normalized residue"],"finding":"A3 rewrites the committed baseline value shape in place (dict -> normalized text for description/status/priority), and the plan's reversibility claim only asserts the NEW read path canonicalizes both shapes. It does not assert the POST-ROLLBACK state: entries already written in normalized-string form by A3-era code, then read by reverted pre-A3 code that produced/expected dict-shaped baselines. The rollback boundary covers forward-reads-of-old-data but not old-reader-of-forward-written-data.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ef9f15f1bcd8f45","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Compatibility and rollback: 'A3 is reversible because the read path canonicalizes both shapes idempotently'; Scope child A3","norm_id":"nf2ff5c8e84d534c1","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A3 ships; several reconciler passes write normalized-string baselines into bindings.json; an incident forces a revert to pre-A3 reconciler code, which now reads string-shaped baselines its comparison path assumed were dict-shaped -> mis-verdict or fail-closed on a baseline it can no longer parse"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to the Compatibility/rollback section (and an AC) that A3 normalization is verified reversible in BOTH directions: run the pre-A3 com